      "question": "What has Brad built on mobile?",
      "answer": "Brad has built a range of mobile work across several roles. At Hopper, Brad co-architected and built RemoteUI, a server-driven UI framework rendered natively with Jetpack Compose and MVVM on Android and SwiftUI on iOS. At Bottle Rocket, Brad shipped native Android apps in Java and Kotlin for brands including Coca-Cola Freestyle, AskPETMD, Starwood SPG and Chewy. At BookShout, Brad rebuilt the ebook reader on a recycled-WebView architecture for more efficient navigation and rendering. Brad's own product, VINDecoded, is one product on three platforms. A React web app runs in the browser and inside both mobile apps. Native Android (Kotlin) and iOS (SwiftUI) shells add what the web can't do.",
